### By design / accepted

The following were audited and confirmed as intentional:

- `applyPilotHeardInstruction` `else →` — documented opt-in; sealed on intermediate types
- `FLY_DOWNWIND` instant completion — not vestigial; completes on physical leg
- `SimState.aircraft: LinkedHashMap` — deterministic iteration order requirement
- `SimRandom` uses `String.hashCode()` — Kotlin stdlib guarantees MPP-stable hash
- Hold-short conflates arrival/constraint — deferred, needs belief-delta work first
- Cancel-takeoff has no readback guard — intentional; safety commands bypass readback horizon
- Airspace boundary geometry — out of current FM scope
- `DEP-CANCEL-TAKEOFF` missing readback guard — intentional for time-critical safety command
- DFA conformance test — already done (`DfaConformanceTest.kt`)
